      "summary": "The provided text contains detailed financial tables from Freeport-McMoRan Inc.'s (FCX) reports, specifically focusing on **Product Revenues and Production Costs** for various mining segments across different periods.\n\n### Key Segments Covered:\n1. **South America Mining**\n   - Includes Cerro Verde and other operations.\n   - Data presented for:\n     - Three Months Ended September 30, 2017\n     - Nine Months Ended September 30, 2018\n     - Nine Months Ended September 30, 2017\n   - Metrics include revenues, production costs, depreciation & amortization (DD&A), unit net cash costs, and gross profit per pound of copper.\n   - Notes mention adjustments for prior period open sales, treatment charges, royalties, and nonrecurring items like Cerro Verde's new three-year CLA.\n\n2. **Indonesia Mining**\n   - Includes Grasberg operations (copper, gold, silver).\n   - Data presented for:\n     - Three Months Ended September 30, 2018 & 2017\n     - Nine Months Ended September 30, 2018 & 2017\n   - Metrics include revenues, production costs, DD&A, unit net cash (credits) costs, and gross profit per pound/ounce.\n   - Notes highlight gold/silver credits, export duties, royalties, and intercompany transactions with PT Smelting.\n\n3. **Molybdenum Mines**\n   - Data presented for:\n     - Three Months Ended September 30, 2018 & 2017\n     - Nine Months Ended September 30, 2018 & 2017\n   - Metrics include revenues, production costs, DD&A, unit net cash costs, and gross profit/loss per pound.\n   - Notes clarify that sales are to FCX's molybdenum sales company at market-based pricing.\n\n### Consolidated Reconciliation:\n- Each segment table includes a reconciliation to amounts reported in FCX's consolidated financial statements.\n- Categories include \"Other mining\" (North America, Indonesia, Molybdenum, Rod & Refining, Atlantic Copper Smelting & Refining) and \"Corporate, other & eliminations.\"\n\n### Important Notes:\n- **Footnotes (a, b, c)** provide context on silver/molybdenum sales, nonrecurring charges (e.g., Cerro Verde royalties), and definitions of \"Other mining.\"\n- **Unit Costs**: Calculated as total costs divided by production volume (e.g., pounds of copper or ounces of gold/silver).\n- **Gross Profit**: Derived after deducting all costs from revenues, including adjustments for prior period sales.\n\nThis data is crucial for analyzing FCX's operational performance, cost structure, and profitability across its key mining regions and commodities.",
