      "sourceUrl": "https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/831259/000083125915000037/",
      "summary": "The provided text contains detailed financial tables from Freeport-McMoRan (FCX) reports for three distinct business segments: **Africa Mining**, **Molybdenum Mines**, and **U.S. Oil & Gas Operations**. The data covers periods including the three months ended June 30, 2014 and 2015, as well as six-month periods ending June 30, 2014 and 2015.\n\n**Key Observations:**\n\n1.  **Africa Mining (Copper & Cobalt):** \n    *   Shows significant revenue fluctuations between the three-month and six-month periods across different years.\n    *   For example, in the six months ended June 30, 2015, total revenues were $783 million, with gross profit of $206 million. In contrast, for the same period in 2014, revenues were $758 million with a higher gross profit of $281 million.\n    *   Unit costs and prices vary significantly between periods (e.g., Gross profit per pound of copper dropped from $1.39/lb in H1 2014 to $0.87/lb in H1 2015).\n\n2.  **Molybdenum Mines:**\n    *   This segment shows a notable loss in the three months ended June 30, 2015 ($7 million loss), compared to a profit of $65 million in the same period in 2014.\n    *   The six-month data for H1 2015 also reflects a small loss ($3 million) versus a profit of $93 million in H1 2014.\n    *   Prices per pound fluctuated, with H1 2014 showing a gross profit of $3.48/lb compared to a loss of $0.09/lb in H1 2015.\n\n3.  **U.S. Oil & Gas Operations:**\n    *   This segment experienced substantial impairment charges, particularly in the six-month periods (e.g., $5.79 billion impairment in H1 2015 vs. $2.686 billion in H1 2014).\n    *   Revenues and realized prices show volatility; for instance, total revenues before derivatives were $1,002 million in H1 2015 but $2,616 million in H1 2014.\n    *   The segment reported a gross loss of $6.3 billion in H1 2015 due to impairments and other costs, whereas H1 2014 showed a gross profit of $625 million.\n\n**Overall Trends:**\nThe data highlights significant year-over-year changes in profitability, primarily driven by commodity price fluctuations, operational costs, and large impairment charges in the oil & gas sector. The molybdenum segment also faced challenges in 2015 compared to 2014.",
